>>
Rule 1 (input values should lie strictly within the real-domain interval to avoid infinities)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (v_1 > -1) ∧ (v_1 < 1)
>>
Rule 2 (exclude exact singularities at ±1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (v_1 ≠ 1) ∧ (v_1 ≠ -1)
>>
Rule 3 (any-rank tensor is allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (all shape dimensions are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
